N cem.pkg
D 16 Apr 2026
U 3
d 'CEM': module to perform Coarsened Exact Matching
d 
d  The cem package provides a Stata implementation of coarsened
d exact matching, a new method for improving the estimation of
d causal effects by reducing  imbalance in covariates between
d treated and control groups.  Coarsened exact matching is faster,
d is easier to use and understand,  requires fewer assumptions, is
d more easily automated, and possesses more  attractive statistical
d properties for many applications than do existing  matching
d methods. In coarsened exact matching, users temporarily coarsen
d their  data, exact match on these coarsened data, and then run
d their analysis on  the uncoarsened, matched data. Coarsened exact
d matching bounds the degree  of model dependence and causal effect
d estimation error by ex ante user choice,  is monotonic imbalance
d bounding (so that reducing the maximum imbalance on  one variable
d has no effect on others), does not require a separate procedure
d to restrict data to common support, meets the congruence
d principle,  is approximately invariant to measurement error,
d balances all nonlinearities and  interactions in sample (i.e.,
d not merely in expectation), and works with  multiply imputed
d datasets. Other matching methods inherit many of the coarsened
d exact matching method's properties when applied to further match
d data preprocessed by coarsened exact matching.
d 
d KW: imbalance
d KW: matching
d KW: coarsened exact matching
d KW: inference
d 
d Requires: Stata version 10.1
d 
d Distribution-Date: 20200215
d 
d Author:  Matthew Blackwell, Harvard University
d Support: email mblackwell@@gov.harvard.edu
d 
d Author: Stefano Iacus, University of Milan
d Support: email
d 
d Author: Gary King, Harvard University
d Support: email
d 
d Author: Giuseppe Porro, University of Trieste
d Support: email
d 
f c\cem.ado
f c\cem.sthlp
f i\imb.ado
f i\imb.sthlp
f l\listwise.ado
f l\listwise.sthlp
f l\lcem.mlib
f c\cem-mata.do
e
